Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 18 03:58:36 2026 +0000

    Signals: no train let into two-way track a train is coming the other way on, or let into from its far end
    
    The user's complex map (2026-11-18, src/play/bugmaps/reports/): plain and path
    signals cleared each train into a free block, and two lines' trains were let
    into one stretch of single track from its two ends (on main, Blue leaving the
    school east and Purple leaving the town west in the same second) and stood nose
    to nose between the signals for good.
    
    A signal clear for a train now also asks for the two-way track its way takes
    beyond it: through its next stop and on to the stop after, up to the first
    passing place long enough for it (a loop's road in sections' topology for its
    length, as the single-line rule for managed lines passes at; one too short for it
    isn't one). Red for it if a train is on that track coming the other way (its
    front leaving a piece by the end this one would come onto it by), or has been let
    into it from the far end and is still asking (a claim). Trains ask one by one in
    a tick, so of two coming at once the first asked goes. A plain signal shows that
    red. Always green, set by the player, lets it by.
    
    - src/sim/two-way.ts: the stretch type and the head-on test.
    - Sim.twoWayGate (beside signalGate): the economy's stretch for a train past a
      signal (`Economy.twoWayStretch`, kept till its stops or the track change).
    - The claim lapses two ticks after its train stops asking. Held while the train
      is on the stretch instead, two trains standing at stops on each other's long
      stretch waited on each other for good (17 jams, 458 arrivals on save 1).
    
    Complex map, each jam cleared as the player would (one of the two put back at
    its first stop 60 s after 30 s stuck), 1800 s:
    - save 1: 4 jams, 547 arrivals (main: 11, 511)
    - save 2: 6 jams, 427 arrivals (main: 19, 430)
    No invariant broken. The jams left are mostly the two longest trains (Blue
    456 mm, Passengers 440 mm): the map's one passing loop (432 and 499 mm roads)
    holds trains up to about 420 mm.
    
    Test (src/sim/two-way.test.ts): save 1, Purple put away and put back at its mill
    at 120 s, 600 s: no invariant broken, no train stands a minute, every train
    comes to its stops. On main: a train stands 449 s (the head-on at 152 s).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
